# Local evaluation reports. Only the directory the harness writes runs into is
# ignored: the rest of `.medharness/` may hold configuration and manifests that
# belong in history.
/.medharness/eval-runs/

# Personal career material derived from this project — resume framings and an
# interview question bank. It describes the repository, so it lives beside the
# checkout, but it is one person's job-search working material rather than
# project documentation, and it must not reach the published docs site. The
# public technical documentation is `docs/medharness-*.md`.
/.career/

# VitePress writes a timestamped copy of its config while the documentation site
# is built, and `doc-sync` runs that build. The copy is build residue with a
# unique name, so it cannot be committed as source and would otherwise reappear
# in `git status` after every documentation run.
website/.vitepress/*.timestamp-*.mjs
